## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical lightweight baseline building for text routing under strict latency constraints, in a data-scarce regime with model calibration requirements. Also covers drift monitoring and retraining cadence.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight text representation with a fixed 30-feature vector
- SGD-based multiclass logistic regression or tiny decision tree for efficiency
- Calibration via temperature scaling
- Drift detection using rolling holdout validation
- Deployment latency and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Training loop outline for SGD multiclass LR
const model = new SGDLogisticRegression({
  learningRate: 0.01,
  epochs: 100,
  batchSize: 32
});
model.fit(XTrain, yTrain);
// Temperature scaling for calibration
const temp = calibrateTemperature(model, XVal, yVal);
// Inference
const predict = (features) => {
  const start = performance.now();
  const probs = model.predictProb(features, temp);
  const latency = performance.now() - start;
  return { probs, latency };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design an online, latency-constrained text classifier with limited features and simple drift checks, testing hashing-based features, SGD/partial_fit, and streaming evaluation.

## Key Concepts
- Hashing-based text features (30 features)
- Online learning with partial_fit
- Latency constraints on CPU
- Drift checks and calibration
- Evaluation metrics for spam detection (precision, recall, F1, PR-AUC)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple online logistic regression with partial_fit (conceptual)
class OnlineLR {
  constructor(nFeatures){ this.w = new Float64Array(nFeatures); this.b = 0; }
  predict(x){ let s=this.b; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) s+= this.w[i]*x[i]; return 1/(1+Math.exp(-s)); }
  partial_fit(x,y,lr=0.1){ const p=this.predict(x); const g=y-p; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) this.w[i]+=lr*g*x[i]; this.b+=lr*g; }
}
```

